## Huntington Beach Lemon Law and Used Vehicles

California lemon law does extend to used vehicles, but the protections are more limited and time-sensitive. Here’s what you need to know:

## Dealership Warranty

Many used vehicles come with a limited dealership warranty, which is often valid for 30 days or 1,000 miles, whichever comes first. If your vehicle experiences qualifying defects during this period, it may be covered under CA lemon law.

## Your Rights

Per California lemon law, dealerships are required to cover repair or provide a buyback of a used lemon vehicle. The warrantor pays any legal fees.

## Did You Buy the Vehicle “As Is”?

Purchasing a vehicle “as is” generally means you’re accepting it with all existing issues and may not be protected under lemon law. However, the dealership must clearly display the “as is” disclaimer on the buyer’s guide at the time of sale. If this was not done properly, you could still qualify for protection. A California lemon law lawyer can help determine if your rights were violated.

